<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herbert II, Count of Vermandois</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 880–943</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herbert II, Count of Vermandois, was a Carolingian descendant and the most powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the 920s. He held King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a> prisoner at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peronne">Péronne</a> from 923 until the king's death in 929 and secured the archbishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a> for his young son. His family's lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picardy">Picardy</a> and Champagne later formed the core of the County of Champagne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herbert-ii-count-of-vermandois.jpg" alt="Herbert II, Count of Vermandois" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis4_Herbert2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
